<title>LEBANON: All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</title>
<headline>All Lebanese t-bill yields fall.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>All yields fell on Lebanese treasury bills, according to weekly rates issued by the Bank of Lebanon on Monday.</p>
<p>It announced the following interest rates for its March 6 issues (previous week in brackets):</p>
<p>    Term		     Discount		     Yield</p>
<p>				(percent)		   (percent)</p>
<p>    Three months	  13.38 (13.41)	     13.84 (13.87)</p>
<p>    Six months	    13.59 (13.62)	     14.58 (14.61)</p>
<p>    12 months	     13.23 (13.25)	     15.24 (15.27)</p>
<p>    24 months   (Interest payable twice yearly) 16.12 (16.14)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (961 1) 602057 745307 745308</p>
</text>
